// milestone: M3
// expect-exit@wasm: 75
// expect-stderr@wasm: `Worker` is not available on target `wasm`
// expect-exit@native: 75
// expect-stderr@native: `Worker` is not available on target `native`
// spec: RFC 0002 §2.9, §7; design §17.271 (9); plan web-apis.md phase 11 ("native green or refusing at startup with the message")
// Spec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#dom-worker

// `main` declares `Worker`, so the host installs `Worker.host()`, whose live workers only the
// JS host has yet (plan phase 11a): WASM and native stop at startup, exit 75 with one line
// naming the effect, before `main` runs, as native does for `Http`. `main` performs nothing, so
// the JS run, which starts no worker, prints nothing and exits 0. `Worker.inline()` inside `main`
// runs everywhere (`worker_inline_roundtrip`).
import std/worker.{Worker}

pub fn main() -> Unit ! {Worker} {}
